## Observable Behavior

The detection is based on observable network behavior rather than a specific security-testing tool or command.

During the controlled simulation:

```text
Source:
10.10.20.10 / KALI01

Destination:
10.10.10.1 / FW01

Protocol:
TCP

Destination Ports:
20-100

Unique Destination Ports:
81

Firewall Action:
BLOCK
```

Although Nmap was used to generate the activity, DET-001 does **not** specifically detect Nmap.

Instead, DET-001 detects the underlying behavior:

```text
Single Source
      |
      v
Single Destination
      |
      v
Large Number of Unique TCP Ports
      |
      v
Short Time Window
      |
      v
Potential Network Service Discovery
```

This allows the detection logic to identify similar reconnaissance behavior regardless of which scanning utility generates the traffic.

