## Positive ATT&CK Validation

A controlled TCP scan was generated from KALI01:

```bash
nmap -sT -Pn -p 20-100 10.10.10.1
```

The test generated activity across:

```text
81 unique TCP destination ports
```

DET-001 threshold:

```text
>=20 unique destination ports
```

Result:

```text
81 >= 20

DET-001 TRIGGERED
```

The scheduled Splunk alert also successfully triggered from the controlled test activity.

This confirmed that DET-001 successfully identified behavior consistent with **T1046 — Network Service Discovery**.

---

## Negative Validation

A smaller TCP scan was generated to validate that limited multi-port activity would remain below the detection threshold.

```bash
nmap -sT -Pn -p 80,443,445,3389 10.10.10.1
```

This generated activity across:

```text
4 unique TCP destination ports
```

DET-001 threshold:

```text
>=20 unique destination ports
```

Result:

```text
4 < 20

DET-001 NOT TRIGGERED
```

This demonstrated that limited multi-port activity did not automatically generate DET-001.

